      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not advisable to mix ibuprofen with omeprazole unless specifically instructed by a healthcare professional. Both medications can affect the stomach lining and interact. I recommend consulting your doctor or dentist about how to treat your toothache safely, especially since omeprazole can mask some symptoms. In the meantime, you may want to try a cold compress on your gum to help with the pain.",
